### Seed demo requests for Railway deployment
# Base URL
# https://xlerion-leaderboard-api-production.up.railway.app

### 1) Create LATAM player
POST https://xlerion-leaderboard-api-production.up.railway.app/api/Players
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "demo_latam",
  "displayName": "Demo LATAM",
  "region": "LATAM"
}

### 2) Create NA player
POST https://xlerion-leaderboard-api-production.up.railway.app/api/Players
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "demo_na",
  "displayName": "Demo NA",
  "region": "NA"
}

### 3) Create EU player
POST https://xlerion-leaderboard-api-production.up.railway.app/api/Players
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "demo_eu",
  "displayName": "Demo EU",
  "region": "EU"
}

# --- Scores ---
# After running the three player creation requests above, copy the returned `Id` values
# and replace the placeholders `{{LATAM_ID}}`, `{{NA_ID}}`, `{{EU_ID}}` in the requests below.

### 4) Submit score (LATAM)
POST https://xlerion-leaderboard-api-production.up.railway.app/api/Scores
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "playerId": {{LATAM_ID}},
  "gameId": "xlerion-arena",
  "value": 85,
  "level": 7,
  "sessionDurationSeconds": 420.5,
  "metadata": "{ \"mode\": \"solo\" }"
}

### 5) Submit score (NA)
POST https://xlerion-leaderboard-api-production.up.railway.app/api/Scores
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "playerId": {{NA_ID}},
  "gameId": "xlerion-arena",
  "value": 120,
  "level": 9,
  "sessionDurationSeconds": 300.0,
  "metadata": "{ \"mode\": \"ranked\" }"
}

### 6) Submit score (EU)
POST https://xlerion-leaderboard-api-production.up.railway.app/api/Scores
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "playerId": {{EU_ID}},
  "gameId": "xlerion-arena",
  "value": 60,
  "level": 4,
  "sessionDurationSeconds": 150.2,
  "metadata": null
}

### 7) Submit another score (LATAM)
POST https://xlerion-leaderboard-api-production.up.railway.app/api/Scores
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "playerId": {{LATAM_ID}},
  "gameId": "xlerion-arena",
  "value": 130,
  "level": 10,
  "sessionDurationSeconds": 500.0,
  "metadata": "{ \"special\": \"combo\" }"
}

### 8) Submit another score (NA)
POST https://xlerion-leaderboard-api-production.up.railway.app/api/Scores
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "playerId": {{NA_ID}},
  "gameId": "xlerion-arena",
  "value": 95,
  "level": 6,
  "sessionDurationSeconds": 260.0,
  "metadata": null
}

# --- Unlock achievements ---
# We unlock two achievements that SeedData ensures exist: FIRST_BLOOD and CENTURION

### 9) Unlock FIRST_BLOOD for LATAM
POST https://xlerion-leaderboard-api-production.up.railway.app/api/Achievements/unlock
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "playerId": {{LATAM_ID}},
  "gameId": "xlerion-arena",
  "achievementCode": "FIRST_BLOOD"
}

### 10) Unlock CENTURION for NA
POST https://xlerion-leaderboard-api-production.up.railway.app/api/Achievements/unlock
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "playerId": {{NA_ID}},
  "gameId": "xlerion-arena",
  "achievementCode": "CENTURION"
}

# Notes
# - Run requests in order. The player creation responses include the created player object with its generated `Id`.
# - Replace the {{LATAM_ID}}, {{NA_ID}}, {{EU_ID}} placeholders with the actual numeric Ids returned
#   from the create requests before running the score/achievement requests.
# - If you prefer automation, I can add a tiny PowerShell script to run these in sequence and extract IDs automatically.
